MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_001: Hm... Where shall I go today? I would so love to\nfind something that could help me remember...
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_002: Ah, Fianna. Funny seeing you here. What's on your\nagenda for the day?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_003: Oh, hello, Lysander... I was just going for a walk\nto nowhere in particular.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_004: I've been hoping to find something that might trigger\na lost memory, so I've been wandering all over.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_005: I see. You sound like you're having a hard time of it.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_006: I can't abandon you to your own devices. So I shall\naccompany you on this errand.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_007: Oh... You will?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_008: I want to help you recover your memories however\nI can.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_009: Oh. Alright then. I appreciate your assistance...
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_010: Maybe seeing something you like will jog your\nmemory. What kinds of things do you enjoy?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_011: Let me see... I like the theater...and poetry.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_012: Ah, so you appreciate taking in verse. A fine hobby.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_013: How about a play, in that case? There's a production\nof Rude Is Right, and Right Is Rude going on.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_014: Um... Just us two?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_015: What's that commotion over there? Some sort of\ndispute? Wait...that's one of my troops!
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_016: He's a very righteous man. He may have gotten\nhimself caught up in trying to mediate.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_017: Then you ought to go to his aid right away.\nYou needn't worry about me.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_018: But...we haven't made any progress yet. I couldn't\nlive with myself if I abandoned you here.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_019: Don't trouble yourself. I get the feeling I'm used\nto this sort of thing.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_020: I see. A thousand apologies, then.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_021: Again today, I remember nothing... I must be getting\nback soon.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_022: I found you at last, Fianna! Sorry I'm so late.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_023: Lysander? I thought you'd already gone.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_024: I went looking for you after finishing my business.\nI was determined to see you off before the sun set.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_025: I see... Thank you.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_026: If you don't mind, why don't we go for another stroll\nsometime? It shall be a day all your own.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_C_027: A whole day...all for me? Hehehe. I'll be there.\nYou have my word.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_001: I wonder if Lysander has arrived... Oh, who's that\nhe's with?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_002: As I have told you, I'm keeping an appointment with\nsomeone else today.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_003: Don't worry about that. C'mon... Let's say you and\nI get to know each other, huh?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_004: My apologies, Lysander... Am I late?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_005: Fianna! Not at all. The day is still young.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_006: This is the woman you're waiting to meet? You like\nthe gloomy, quiet types, hm?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_007: And what, I suppose you think you're entitled to his\ntime and attention?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_008: That's rather rude of you. Whatever you assume she\nis, I tell you, she is not.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_009: I may be quiet, and I may be gloomy, but I will not\nhave you disparage this man for honoring his word.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_010: He has promised himself to me for the day, so yes,\nI am entitled—and I've come to claim what is mine.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_011: Fine... Calm down. I'm going.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_012: Thank you, Fianna. She's been rather insistent lately,\nto the point where it's a problem.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_013: I'm impressed that you drove her off. You sounded\nquite fierce.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_014: Where did that come from? It felt like something\nI'd done before...
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_015: Could it have been before you lost your memories?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_016: Ah! It just may be.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_017: A breakthrough at last! At this rate, you'll be well on\nyour way to recovering those memories.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_018: {SetColor=Gray}But the force behind those words... Was this who\nFianna was before the amnesia?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_019: {SetColor=Gray}She was like a different woman entirely. If that\nwoman returns, what of the Fianna I know?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_020: Lysander? What's the matter?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_021: Er, sorry about that. Tell me—what do you think\nyou'd do once your memories returned?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_022: Well... If I can, I'd like to thank everyone who has\ntaken care of me.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_023: Especially Centurio, who protected me as if I were\nhis own daughter—and the many others besides.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_025: I'm grateful for you too, Lysander. When my memory\ndoes return, we can talk all about it over coffee.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_026: Ah! By all means, let's have a toast.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_027: Though...does it have to be coffee?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_028: Is there...a problem? Have you had your fill of me?
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_029: No, no! Not at all. If coffee is what you want,\nI'll be happy to raise a mug with you.
MID_SE_Fia_Lys_B_030: Heeheehee. Is that so? I'm so glad to hear it.
